                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pure distilled Saturday morning cartoon energy in JRPG form, and it absolutely rules. You play a total nerd who gets a magic Trapper Keeper and starts turning everyday objects into weapons while fighting evil robots, bullies, and cartoon villains. The references come thick and fast (and they’re actually funny), the combat has that perfect Paper Mario style timing spice, and the soundtrack by Vince DiCola is ridiculously good. It’s short, sweet, full of heart, and dripping with nostalgia without ever feeling mean spirited.",
